# Figma design implementation

Apply this rule when UI work is driven by a Figma design (link, frame, or component spec).

## Figma MCP

1. Use **Figma MCP** tools to inspect the file: frames, components, typography, colors, spacing, and export hints.
2. Prefer accurate layout tokens from Figma over guessing from screenshots alone.
3. If Figma MCP is unavailable, say so and ask the user to connect OAuth or reload Cursor after MCP sync.

## Skills and plugins

- Prefer **`/add-plugin figma`** (Figma plugin/skills bundle) when starting Figma-driven UI tasks — it adds structured workflows for design-to-code.
- Reuse existing design-system components in the repo before creating one-off styles.

## After implementation

- When feasible, run a **Playwright** (or browser MCP) check: key screens render, critical interactions work, and layout matches the design at a reasonable breakpoint.
- Playwright verification is recommended, not required on every small tweak — use judgment for scope.

## Scope

This rule is **not** mandatory every chat — only when Figma links or explicit design-from-Figma requests appear.
